function outro_sec_screenwriter_5(co)
hss.evt(co,"{CONNECTED_CHARACTER_NAME} reads through the email from Crown Studios in disbelief.", "")
hss.dlgA(co,"{CONNECTED_CHARACTER}","~'Upon further consideration, we've decided that your screenplay is not a good fit for Crown Studios. Best of luck...'~",4)
hss.dlgA(co,"{CONNECTED_CHARACTER}","I can't believe this! I used every one of their ideas! How can they suddenly not like it when I made the changes that ~they~ suggested?",2)
hss.dlgA(co,hss.U,"Maybe... because not all of their ideas were good ones.",2)
hss.dlgA(co,"{CONNECTED_CHARACTER}","But if a studio tells me to change something, how can I just say no?",2)
hss.dlg(co,hss.U,"It's your screenplay, and you're the one who knows it best. A big part of your job is knowing which suggestions are good, and which ones aren't.")
hss.dlg(co,hss.U,"I know I said you'd have to make some changes... but when you get right down to it, ~your~ voice is what made this screenplay great. With so many people trying to contribute, your voice got lost in the din.")
hss.dlgA(co,"{CONNECTED_CHARACTER}","You're right. Ugh, I guess this screenplay's a lost cause.",2)
hss.dlg(co,hss.U,"Don't give up on it just yet. I know a business-savvy guy who can help you make sense of all this.")
hss.evt(co,"You make a phone call, and a few hours later you and {CONNECTED_CHARACTER_NAME} meet Ethan in his dorm.", "")
hss.dlgA(co,hss.E,"So ~this~ is the visionary {CONNECTED_CHARACTER_NAME}. I read your screenplay, and--",1)
hss.dlgA(co,"{CONNECTED_CHARACTER}","Please don't say you loved it and then later decide you hate it. I don't know if my heart can survive another ride on that roller coaster.",2)
hss.dlg(co,hss.E,"Yeah... I heard about the Crown Studios business. Studio execs usually mean well, but you've gotta learn to speak their language.")
hss.dlg(co,hss.E,"Sometimes, when they say 'set this on Mars', it's executive-speak for 'let's see if we can come up with a more interesting setting'.")
hss.dlgA(co,"{CONNECTED_CHARACTER}","That... makes a lot of sense, actually.",4)
hss.dlg(co,hss.U,"So what's your verdict, Ethan? Think this project is salvageable?")
hss.evt(co,"Ethan takes both drafts of {CONNECTED_CHARACTER_NAME}'s screenplay out of his briefcase and lays them on his desk.", "")
hss.dlg(co,hss.E,"We've got two extremes here. One draft has a great concept and a streamlined, compelling plot, but a pretty underdeveloped world and unremarkable characters.")
hss.dlg(co,hss.E,"The other draft is big and exciting with characters that leap off the page... but it's overcomplicated. The action scenes have become so bloated they're crowding out the plot.")
hss.evt(co,"Ethan points to a spot on the desk, right between both screenplays.", "")
hss.dlg(co,hss.E,"Right ~here...~ is a gritty, understated, character-driven thriller that people will line up around the block to see.")
hss.evt(co,"{CONNECTED_CHARACTER_NAME} looks from one draft to the other, then focuses somewhere in the middle.", "")
hss.dlg(co,"{CONNECTED_CHARACTER}","Okay, then... sounds like I have a gritty, understated, character-driven thriller to write.")
hss.showQuestComplete(co)
hss.evt(co,"A few days later, you and Ethan head to the Screenwriter Dorm to read the latest draft of {CONNECTED_CHARACTER_NAME}'s screenplay.", "")
hss.dlgA(co,"{CONNECTED_CHARACTER}","...so? Is it any good?",2)
hss.dlgA(co,hss.E,"It's ~all~ good, {CONNECTED_CHARACTER_NAME}.",1)
hss.dlgA(co,hss.U,"I love the new setting! 1920s Yukon presents way more specific and interesting challenges than generic present-day forest.",1)
hss.dlgA(co,"{CONNECTED_CHARACTER}","It was a lot of research to make sure all the technology, dialect, and place names were authentic, but it makes the story feel so much more ~real!~",1)
hss.dlg(co,hss.E,"Definitely. And good job scaling back the action to let the romance shine through. You actually had me tearing up a little during the confession scene!")
hss.dlg(co,"{CONNECTED_CHARACTER}","Somewhere along the line, I really drifted away from this project. But this new draft... it feels right. It feels like it's really ~mine~ again.")
hss.dlg(co,hss.U,"That's what I like to hear! This is a really amazing screenplay, {CONNECTED_CHARACTER_NAME}.")
hss.dlgA(co,"{CONNECTED_CHARACTER}","Thanks. It's too bad I already blew my chance with Crown Studios. My friend made it pretty clear that they weren't interested in seeing any more of this screenplay.",2)
hss.dlg(co,hss.E,"Hey, you've done a lot of good work on this, {CONNECTED_CHARACTER_NAME}, and you should be proud of that. This chance didn't work out, but more will come along.")
hss.dlgA(co,hss.E,"For now, I think we all deserve to go out and have a little fun. There's an industry party I was planning to hit up tonight. What do you say? Be my plus twos?",7)
end
function outro_sec_screenwriter_6(co)
hss.evt(co,"At the party, you mingle with industry professionals on the patio of a gorgeous bungalow in Pasadena.", "")
hss.evt(co,"{CONNECTED_CHARACTER_NAME} sips at a glass of sangria, nodding along with the soft music that just barely rises above the hum of conversation.", "")
hss.dlg(co,"{CONNECTED_CHARACTER}","~This~ is a Hollywood industry party? I didn't think it'd be so... chill!")
hss.dlg(co,hss.U,"Hey, even famous people like a good low-pressure hangout once in a while.")
hss.evt(co,"Ethan emerges from the crowd, throwing an arm around {CONNECTED_CHARACTER_NAME}'s shoulders.", "")
hss.dlgA(co,hss.E,"~There's~ our star on the rise! I just happened to run into the head of this ~fantastic~ little indie studio by the punch bowl, and do you know what he said?",1)
hss.dlg(co,"{CONNECTED_CHARACTER}","Uh... no?")
hss.dlgA(co,hss.E,"He said that he's so sick of these big cookie-cutter action movies. The whole reason he started this studio was so he could really push the envelope and tell stories that were more personal.",1)
hss.dlg(co,hss.E,"And then ~I~ told him about this amazing screenplay I just read. Two friends, fighting for their lives in the Canadian wilderness, realize that they would each die to save the other.")
hss.dlgA(co,hss.U,"I'm guessing he liked it? You've got 'Ethan just made something happen' face.",1)
hss.dlgA(co,hss.E,"Ethan just cracked the door open. Now ~{CONNECTED_CHARACTER_NAME}~ is gonna make something happen.",1)
hss.dlgA(co,"{CONNECTED_CHARACTER}","I... I am? I mean ~thank you!~ I--",4)
hss.evt(co,"Ethan gives {CONNECTED_CHARACTER_NAME} a little shove, pointing to a man in his mid-thirties wearing a t-shirt and slacks.", "")
hss.dlgA(co,hss.E,"Go. Schmooze.",1)
hss.showQuestComplete(co)
hss.evt(co,"A while later, {CONNECTED_CHARACTER_NAME} finds you leaning against the patio railing, looking out over the city.", "")
hss.dlg(co,hss.U,"So? How'd it go?")
hss.dlg(co,"{CONNECTED_CHARACTER}","Well, my movie probably isn't going to be a summer blockbuster... and this budget is a few zeroes smaller than the last offer, but...")
hss.dlgA(co,hss.U,"But what? Out with it already!",1)
hss.dlgA(co,"{CONNECTED_CHARACTER}","He wants to make the movie! ~My~ movie! The more we talked, the more excited we both got about the story! We're totally on the same wavelength.",1)
hss.dlg(co,"{CONNECTED_CHARACTER}","And I realized, that's what I really wanted all along. I don't care about the big-name studios or the A-list stars. As long as I get to see ~my~ baby on the big screen, it'll all be worth it.")
hss.dlg(co,hss.U,"And you know, this is only your first movie. If you ~did~ want a blockbuster, there's always the next one.")
hss.dlgA(co,"{CONNECTED_CHARACTER}","Yeah... thanks to you, now I've got my foot in the door.",1)
hss.dlgA(co,"{CONNECTED_CHARACTER}","This is only the beginning. Who knows what'll happen in the next chapter?",1)
hss.dlgA(co,"{CONNECTED_CHARACTER}","Thank you, {YOU}. When this movie comes out, I'm putting your name in the credits, right next to mine.",1)
hss.dlgA(co,hss.U,"That'd be an honor, {CONNECTED_CHARACTER_NAME}.",1)
end
